  "notes": "SV base-game lists are the Paldea-dex version exclusives. Tauros is left out because both versions have a Paldean Tauros breed, so the difference is only a form. Serebii's SV exclusives page lumps the DLC exclusives into one list. They are split here using Dittobase, Prima and VGC plus PokeAPI dex membership. Walking Wake (Scarlet) and Iron Leaves (Violet) are placed under the-indigo-disk because they are Blueberry-dex entries. In-game they have only been obtainable through limited 7-star raids or events, never in the wild. In The Indigo Disk, Vulpix/Ninetales (Scarlet) and Sandshrew/Sandslash (Violet) are exclusive only as their Alolan forms in the Terarium. The Kanto forms of both lines are in the Kitakami dex in both versions. The Snacksworth legendaries in the-indigo-disk lists are soft exclusives. Solo quests give them in only one version, but group Blueberry Quests give the other version's set, so they can be caught in either game with online play. They are not in the Blueberry dex, so they also have extra entries. Urshifu is not listed because it is unconfirmed whether Kubfu can evolve in SV. PokeAPI also lists Pecharunt in the Blueberry dex, so its extra entry is a safety duplicate. BDSP exclusives are Serebii's full list. It includes Grand Underground and Ramanas Park exclusives and some non-Sinnoh-dex species (Electivire, Magmortar, Gliscor, etc.). The Cranidos/Shieldon lines are fossil exclusives, but the fossils themselves can be traded. Grand Underground lists were parsed from Serebii's Pokearth Grand Underground page (all hideaways, all progress stages). Only species not in the original Sinnoh dex are listed, and every one of them first appears at the National Pokedex stage (some also as Rare Spawns). The version split follows each version's spawn tables. The 'Evolve or breed' entries are computed from PokeAPI evolution chains (Gen 1-4 members not in the Sinnoh dex). Their versions come from the chain's Grand Underground or Sinnoh-dex availability. Example: Spheal/Sealeo spawn only in Shining Pearl, but Walrein spawns in both, so they can be bred in Brilliant Diamond. Not covered for BDSP: other post-game non-Sinnoh species from Trophy Garden, Great Marsh, swarms and gifts (e.g. Eevee, Porygon); Heatran, Regigigas, Giratina, Cresselia and Phione; and save-data or event Mythicals (Mew, Jirachi, Darkrai, Shaymin, Arceus). Ramanas Park: Giratina is only fought there, not caught. Serebii lists both Latias and Latios in both versions. | Edited after generation: removed Alolan-form-only Indigo Disk exclusives (Vulpix/Sandshrew lines), moved Snacksworth and Mochi Mayhem entries to the-indigo-disk, normalised methods to the app set. This file is now maintained by hand."
